{"title":"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Proof_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Proof Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(estimated_guess)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (estimated guess)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496ff4bbc8f0b9e2a508898b4740c50b4ebf518b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADEH$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> trisect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> trisect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d19b2b402fd919915fe203abbf4e07664251c82d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{HE}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" />. In addition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/3/bc38f24a95fd88bd541144a7ea24df6f80b7790a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH=AC=2$\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e867467073fae9550c977a21ee2cb19426c4f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=3$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. What is the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> shown in the figure? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/4/614d325a6be5be041b053c50024bd55a65735595.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); pathpen = linewidth(0.7); pointpen = black; pointfontpen = fontsize(10); pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,W,X,Y,Z; A=(0,2); B=(1,2); C=(2,2); D=(3,2); H=(0,0); G=(1,0); F=(2,0); E=(3,0); D(&#39;A&#39;,A, N); D(&#39;B&#39;,B,N); D(&#39;C&#39;,C,N); D(&#39;D&#39;,D,N); D(&#39;E&#39;,E,SE); D(&#39;F&#39;,F,SE); D(&#39;G&#39;,G,SW); D(&#39;H&#39;,H,SW); D(A--F); D(B--E); D(D--G); D(C--H); Z=IP(A--F, C--H); Y=IP(A--F, D--G); X=IP(B--E,D--G); W=IP(B--E,C--H); D(&#39;W&#39;,W,1.6*N); D(&#39;X&#39;,X,1.6*plain.E); D(&#39;Y&#39;,Y,1.6*S); D(&#39;Z&#39;,Z,1.6*plain.W); D(A--D--E--H--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"232\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb37456335d8de5ba08a432c82154637673a508d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\sqrt{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"474\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Symmetry\" title=\"Symmetry\">symmetry</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is a square.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e69e8151c49e0c62ddcaf2e32d408891558b3e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); pathpen = linewidth(0.7); pointpen = black; pointfontpen = fontsize(10); pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,W,X,Y,Z; A=(0,2); B=(1,2); C=(2,2); D=(3,2); H=(0,0); G=(1,0); F=(2,0); E=(3,0); D(&#39;A&#39;,A, N); D(&#39;B&#39;,B,N); D(&#39;C&#39;,C,N); D(&#39;D&#39;,D,N); D(&#39;E&#39;,E,SE); D(&#39;F&#39;,F,SE); D(&#39;G&#39;,G,SW); D(&#39;H&#39;,H,SW); D(A--F); D(B--E); D(D--G); D(C--H); Z=IP(A--F, C--H); Y=IP(A--F, D--G); X=IP(B--E,D--G); W=IP(B--E,C--H); D(&#39;W&#39;,W,1.6*N); D(&#39;X&#39;,X,1.6*plain.E); D(&#39;Y&#39;,Y,1.6*S); D(&#39;Z&#39;,Z,1.6*plain.W); MP(&quot;1&quot;,(A+B)/2,2*N); MP(&quot;2&quot;,(A+H)/2,plain.W); D(B--Z); MP(&quot;1&quot;,(B+Z)/2,plain.W); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}&quot;,(W+Z)/2,plain.SE); D(A--D--E--H--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p>Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed6279f22023a8383cfc839a32e878a4c1e3e2b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BZ}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/3996443794ddc26b46ab069a9195686ef30e300c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BZ = \\frac 12AH = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/260c952a22d2e37aa68822a758f9dba2fb5f40e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BWZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe048f5c1382916a77470eb42a56f76de35b789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45-45-90 \\triangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"114\" height=\"14\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4860e4f3943921fd678f9be1e2ee9ba1ebd2e54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WZ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"84\" height=\"41\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/7092e3fa4c752feddfe44b5b8f4809d3e2bc00f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[WXYZ] = \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^2 =\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"247\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>There are many different similar ways to come to the same conclusion using different <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">45-45-90 triangles</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9844cabb16af8eebe5cd42a6be9927e8d83689f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); pathpen = linewidth(0.7); pointpen = black; pointfontpen = fontsize(10); pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,W,X,Y,Z; A=(0,2); B=(1,2); C=(2,2); D=(3,2); H=(0,0); G=(1,0); F=(2,0); E=(3,0); D(&#39;A&#39;,A, N); D(&#39;B&#39;,B,N); D(&#39;C&#39;,C,N); D(&#39;D&#39;,D,N); D(&#39;E&#39;,E,SE); D(&#39;F&#39;,F,SE); D(&#39;G&#39;,G,SW); D(&#39;H&#39;,H,SW); D(A--F); D(B--E); D(D--G); D(C--H); Z=IP(A--F, C--H); Y=IP(A--F, D--G); X=IP(B--E,D--G); W=IP(B--E,C--H); D(&#39;W&#39;,W,1.6*N); D(&#39;X&#39;,X,1.6*plain.E); D(&#39;Y&#39;,Y,1.6*S); D(&#39;Z&#39;,Z,1.6*plain.W); D(B--D((A+H)/2)--G);D(C--D((E+D)/2)--F); D(A--D--E--H--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"232\" />\n</p><p>Drawing lines as shown above and piecing together the triangles, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is made up of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> squares congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecb9d4c5a9adf027e04a51a2def416d5ed0b7db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[WXYZ] = \\frac{2\\cdot 3}{12} =\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"220\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We see that if we draw a line to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1dae295f7ba255af12a078f5ea4e35c009b82e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> it is half the width of the rectangle so that length would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the resulting triangle is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22231a5cdd4fe05a11f4b577e3b81221f3017a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45-45-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> so using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> we can get that each side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d70a820870539b5b807a6a5ed51acf564d8a6974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{1^2}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"43\" /> so the area of the middle square would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/f/1ff64602684289da873ff155e086440241928eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{\\frac{1^2}{2}})^2=(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}})^2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"223\" height=\"50\" /> which is our answer.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are trisection points and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/286e989082359d570543d0269004ce484008ce68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 2$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f142d92351c7c9e5a27f8a5c133742642df1c495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84d2107ab7da6ef477ebbf010ecff02f5436cb25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = AH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />, so triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a673270b385175f167608a4dac92da48129fb5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACH$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> is a right isosceles triangle, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77b555f89871714f4bbe8ae6cd5d767d6fba9863.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACH = \\angle AHC = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"187\" height=\"13\" />. By symmetry, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154cffe3871a3ef13710844a1a96c55fd9e7d5a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFH$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/65772dfa055c928d9b85ea6be539a35c1dff1b38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEG$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c0afb40c0a08457a36ebab89b23c17b40b9eff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BED$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> are also right isosceles triangles. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e45a20da8cfd012b7aa67ca7c7529acbf8d9cfcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle WAD = \\angle WDA = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"196\" height=\"13\" />, which means triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb35ae52ec6902ca538f725331e7ff70792eade3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AWD$\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is also a right isosceles triangle. Also, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a83f718b5548bdac1f5c7a32217941c1c739ebef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is a right isosceles triangle.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02fcf46f9da86ee3a22d601c6670b1ca0f1c682d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AW = AD/\\sqrt{2} = 3/\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/2/7a2e33462ba74e174220d1153287bbf2ed0fe652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = AC/\\sqrt{2} = 2/\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"21\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24d10b17c7918e974ec1d834921e31f89de268ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XW = AW - AX = 3/\\sqrt{2} - 2/\\sqrt{2} = 1/\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"344\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>By symmetry, quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is a square, so its area is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7bffffa8979e46667515be33212ae261ce29fcc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[XW^2 = \\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\right)^2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{1}{2}}.\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~made by AoPS  (somewhere) -put here by qkddud~\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Proof_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Proof_Bash)\">Solution 5 (Proof Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Proof Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/4/614d325a6be5be041b053c50024bd55a65735595.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); pathpen = linewidth(0.7); pointpen = black; pointfontpen = fontsize(10); pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,W,X,Y,Z; A=(0,2); B=(1,2); C=(2,2); D=(3,2); H=(0,0); G=(1,0); F=(2,0); E=(3,0); D(&#39;A&#39;,A, N); D(&#39;B&#39;,B,N); D(&#39;C&#39;,C,N); D(&#39;D&#39;,D,N); D(&#39;E&#39;,E,SE); D(&#39;F&#39;,F,SE); D(&#39;G&#39;,G,SW); D(&#39;H&#39;,H,SW); D(A--F); D(B--E); D(D--G); D(C--H); Z=IP(A--F, C--H); Y=IP(A--F, D--G); X=IP(B--E,D--G); W=IP(B--E,C--H); D(&#39;W&#39;,W,1.6*N); D(&#39;X&#39;,X,1.6*plain.E); D(&#39;Y&#39;,Y,1.6*S); D(&#39;Z&#39;,Z,1.6*plain.W); D(A--D--E--H--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"232\" />\n</p><p><br />\nBy symmetry, quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is a square. \n</p><p>First step, proving that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c9947f1179085d17337e3ed4660a3714c09019a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BXD \\sim \\triangle BWC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>We can tell quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f3697851303f171d67b875c7a10194b4e33486ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c66b2b2ad94aebbf8cdfc3d5582692e2123359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD \\parallel GH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db2516a16aa71ac3f71e240a42d8ea4b4232527e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD \\cong GH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>By knowing that, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e066244fbffaabc8c95f70f74f7510dd81b1d78c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CW \\parallel DX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Finally, we can now prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c9947f1179085d17337e3ed4660a3714c09019a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BXD \\sim \\triangle BWC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" /> by AA, with a ratio of 2:1.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d552df563ad94258c2bf570377a7a461bca938c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = DE = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd895453b744d8dac7e377cdc7edf66fa624eeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDE = 90$\" width=\"99\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b4072dec30604cbea5998c12fddd9eacfeb564.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is a 45-45-90 triangle. \n</p><p>This will make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/857c312451355388cdcf8f22f363f0e18866b2e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DBE = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"99\" height=\"13\" /> making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/81940750e4a63eaa20ec47d13f9d138bcbb7cdb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BXD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/110c4c107a36a8a011246f1c3240a156edfd974f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BWC$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> a 45-45-90 triangle. \n</p><p>This will make, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c30550b181f57435985f91e86e4abb729c54ce55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 2, BC=1, DX=BX=\\sqrt 2, BW=WX=\\frac{\\sqrt 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"435\" height=\"43\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/434b43c3ed50dfcfe55a5a68619bfe75826a1aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WX$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> is the length of the square, our answer will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/907caf9e4f3e6f5dfb251bba8ebb339213ad6d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{\\sqrt 2}{2})^2 = \\frac{2}{4} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{1}{2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"178\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~ghfhgvghj10\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28estimated_guess.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(estimated_guess)\">Solution 6 (estimated guess)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (estimated guess)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we know that quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is a square, we conclude that its area is a rational number because the side lengths may be irrational. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916ae324e8df00b7856f831d84c16d8ae754e1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf(A)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"46\" height=\"32\" />\n~elpianista227\n</p><p><br />\nNote: elpianista227 forgot to account for the fact that it isn't directly stated in the problem that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is a square. Also, even if we were to say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is a square the side lengths could be some variation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce55298e9e1c0d0dacbc6d61c958f084007aba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Maxisw\" title=\"User:Maxisw\">MisW</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:Maxisw\" title=\"User talk:Maxisw\">talk</a>)\n</p><p>Note: side of square might be to the 4th root or whatever\n- MATH-MATHSTER\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by the Beauty of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GX33rxlJz7s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GX33rxlJz7s</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A\">2006 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a hre